  "data": "figures/data/fig-pathways.json",
  "caption": "Simplified biosynthetic map. Fixed carbon feeds the cytosolic mevalonate (MVA) and plastidic MEP pathways, which make the C5 units of all terpenoids, and the shikimate pathway, which makes phenylalanine and tyrosine for the phenylpropanoid and flavonoid branches. End products are the curated compounds of this site; dashed edges compress several steps, and two edges mark artefacts formed after the plant (carnosol on drying, chamazulene on steam distillation).",
  "how_to_read": "Start at the top with the carbon Rubisco fixes and follow it down one of three trunks. On the terpenoid trunk, the length of the prenyl chain decides the class: ten carbons for the monoterpenes of mint, sage, thyme and basil, fifteen for the sesquiterpenes of chamomile and lemon balm, twenty for rosemary's carnosic acid and thirty for ursolic acid. On the phenolic trunk, phenylalanine becomes cinnamic acid and then p-coumaric acid, which splits three ways: towards rosmarinic acid, towards basil's eugenol and estragole, and, with three malonyl-CoA units, into the flavonoids. Each coloured end node opens its compound page. Every edge carries the reference it was drawn from; hover it to see which.",
  "explain": [
   {
    "on": "MVA / MEP",
    "text": "Two pathways in two compartments make the same C5 building blocks; the plastid route mainly supplies monoterpenes and diterpenes, the cytosolic route sesquiterpenes and triterpenes [110,111]."
   },
   {
    "on": "geranyl diphosphate",
    "text": "The single C10 precursor from which basil, thyme, sage and peppermint synthases make different skeletons [113,114,121]."
   },
   {
    "on": "γ-terpinene → thymol",
    "text": "In thyme the aromatic ring of thymol is made from γ-terpinene by P450 enzymes and a dehydrogenase [42]."
   },
   {
    "on": "matricin → chamazulene",
    "text": "Not a plant step: matricin is at least partly converted to chamazulene during steam distillation [10]."
   },
   {
    "on": "carnosic acid → carnosol",
    "text": "Oxidation after harvest and during drying; carnosol is described as an artefact [43]."
   },
   {
    "on": "rosmarinic acid",
    "text": "Drawn as its two building blocks, caffeic acid and 3,4-dihydroxyphenyllactic acid, from phenylalanine and tyrosine; the enzyme sequence is not shown [118]."
   },
   {
    "on": "chalcone synthase",
    "text": "Condenses one p-coumaroyl-CoA with three malonyl-CoA, the entry to all flavonoids [123]."
   },
   {
    "on": "chrysin branch",
    "text": "A root-specific 4′-deoxyflavone pathway in Scutellaria baicalensis [28]."
   }
  ],
